WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.250
There's more to the "Five Nights at Freddy's"
movie than just creepy mechanical monsters

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.756
and jumpscares, though there are plenty of
those, too.

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:09.278
Let's dig into what all that mayhem really
meant.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.940
The film's protagonist, Mike Schmidt, suffers
from anxiety that's spurred by a traumatic

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.370
incident from his childhood.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.735
When Mike was a kid, his younger brother Garrett
was abducted while they were on a camping trip.

00:00:19.735 --> 00:00:23.915
Now, as an adult, he uses his dreams to figure
out who took him, with no success.

00:00:24.142 --> 00:00:27.580
Not only does this nightmare cause him to
struggle to keep a job, but it also affects

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.440
his relationship with his younger sister Abby,
who he cares for by himself.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.660
Mike's newest job, a seemingly harmless nighttime
security gig at a closed children's party

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.400
venue called Freddy Fazbear's Pizza, quickly
becomes unsettling when the animatronics come

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.560
to life at night.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.884
At first, they appear friendly as they develop
a strong bond with Abby.

00:00:44.884 --> 00:00:49.583
Unfortunately, that's only a ruse so they
can manipulate Mike's desire for answers about Garrett.

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:53.109
The animatronic characters ultimately make
a deal with him for Abby.

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:57.783
Mike regretfully accepts, and the friendly
characters turn violent to please their unseen master.

00:00:57.783 --> 00:01:02.120
Mike is nearly killed by his newfound animatronic
foes, but he's rescued by his friend Vanessa,

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.979
who discloses everything she knows about Freddy's.

00:01:04.979 --> 00:01:07.656
"Have you met them yet?"

00:01:07.656 --> 00:01:08.457
"Met…who?"

00:01:08.457 --> 00:01:12.390
This includes that her father, William Afton,
is the orchestrator of this nightmare, and

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:17.290
that the animatronics that Mike has been dealing
with have a horrific past of their own.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:21.540
Decades ago, Afton, the mysterious owner of
Freddy Fazbear's Pizza, brought Freddy and

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.370
the other animatronics to life by kidnapping
children and stuffing them into the mechanical mascots.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.110
This caused their souls to be intertwined
with the machinery.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.110
Now, Afton controls them through drawings
that influence their beliefs, and is looking

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.844
to add another child, Abby, to his collection.

00:01:35.844 --> 00:01:38.530
"They want to make her like them."

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.000
Now knowing all this, Mike heads back to Freddy
Fazbear's to stop Freddy.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.720
Mike runs into Afton -- who reveals himself
to be the guy who gave Mike this job under

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.740
the name Steve Raglan.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.010
With his own mechanized yellow bunny suit,
Afton senselessly beats Mike.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:55.140
He's only thwarted by Abby, who uses her own
drawings that show Freddy and the others what

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.460
Afton did to them.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.560
She convinces them to betray Afton, just as
the spring traps in his costume cause him

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.939
to be locked in it forever.

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:05.870
As the building falls apart, Freddy and his
companions pull Afton away while Mike and

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.489
Abby help a severely-injured Vanessa escape.

00:02:08.489 --> 00:02:12.580
Some time later, Mike visits Vanessa in the
hospital and shares a family dinner with Abby,

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.060
promising that they could see Freddy again
one day.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.810
Meanwhile, one of the ghost children leaves
Afton behind a locked door so that he suffers

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.360
the same fate as his victims.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.470
At the start of the film, Mike blames himself
for Garrett's abduction, searching for answers

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.330
years after his disappearance.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:31.349
He even recreates and relives Garrett being
taken through his dreams just to find clues.

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:35.730
His frustrations from his failures also drive
him to be incredibly cold towards Abby.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:39.800
He cruelly chastises her for having imaginary
friends, seemingly wishing that Garrett was

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.269
there instead of her.

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:45.399
That's what makes him so vulnerable to the
ghost children who inhabit Freddy and his cronies.

00:02:45.399 --> 00:02:47.755
He nearly loses Abby because of that pain.

00:02:47.755 --> 00:02:51.989
Mike instantly regrets his initial decision
to trade Abby for Garrett, and does everything

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:53.569
he can to fix things.

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:57.220
He realizes that Abby is just as important
to him as Garrett was, and sets out to stop

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.960
Freddy from turning Abby into an animatronic.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:03.690
When Mike gets a moment alone with Abby, he
apologizes for how he treated her and dedicates

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.440
himself to being a better brother.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.430
Based on the film's ending, Mike seems to
live up to that promise.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.860
He now acts as a better parental figure for
Abby, sharing dinner with her just like their

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.130
family used to do.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.580
Mike turns things around for himself and has
the potential for a better relationship with

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.860
Abby, no longer trapped by his guilt.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.330
As Mike finds a sort of redemption, Afton
finally gets punished for his horrible crimes.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.659
In the climactic final battle, Afton is slowly
cut down by the spring traps in his animatronic

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:30.690
suit and becomes stuck inside it.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.780
As he bleeds out and the building falls apart,
he's dragged away.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.239
We don't see what happens to him until the
final scene, where Afton is in one of the backrooms.

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:40.037
The ghost children leave him there for dead.

00:03:40.037 --> 00:03:43.130
He's still alive, but not going anywhere any
time soon.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.640
"The owner's just not ready to let it go yet."

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:50.208
The ghost children, and the mechanical monsters
they inhabit, are no longer under Afton's control.

00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:53.770
Thanks to the picture that Abby draws of Afton
killing the children, the magic bind that

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.590
Afton has over Freddy and the other animatronics
is broken.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:01.217
They're fully able to act on their own, and
it's a key reason why they all turn on Afton in the end.

00:04:01.217 --> 00:04:04.890
Now, Freddy and his friends are more powerful
than Afton, leaving him to the same fate they

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.490
suffered before they died.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:10.060
It's hard to say whether Afton will simply
die now or if this could be the start of his

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.010
return as a larger-than-life nightmare.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.850
But, at least for now, his reign of terror
has come to an end.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:20.840
The personal trauma Mike deals with is the
emotional core of "Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:25.767
The film's depiction of how lingering grief
can lead someone to lose themselves is a horror in itself.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:29.620
Although Mike's erratic behavior and cruel
treatment of Abby make him tough to like at

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.320
first, it's hard not to feel something for
him as his trauma becomes clear.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.630
He's so desperate to find any resolution to
what happened to Garrett that it's the only

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.160
thing he dreams about.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.570
His hunger for the truth runs so deep that
he uses his sleeping pills to fall into a

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.030
deep slumber so that his dreams are more surreal.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:48.479
His residual anxiety causes him to lash out
at others, including a man he mistakenly thinks

00:04:48.479 --> 00:04:50.010
is kidnapping a child.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:53.881
The film's depiction of Mike's stress is easily
relatable to anyone who struggles to let go

00:04:53.881 --> 00:04:56.060
of the past or is haunted by it.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:01.470
It drives him to put Abby in peril and consumes
him so greatly that it detaches from reality entirely.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:05.320
It's what makes Mike's growth so impactful,
and there are some great moments, like Mike's

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.190
apology to Abby and the realization of his
mistakes, that emphasize him coming out of

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.660
his own darkness.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.970
Although "Five Nights at Freddy's" features
five main ghost children who have distinct

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:18.830
connections to Freddy and his machine allies,
there are surely more.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:22.580
Afton clearly has a pattern of abducting children,
and the fact that he took Garrett so long

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.330
ago likely means that he's been doing this
for quite a while.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:29.480
It's very probable that Afton has put other
children into mech suits over the years, and

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:33.169
some of the other characters seen in the background
could signify past attempts.

00:05:33.169 --> 00:05:36.320
In the backroom that characters walk in and
out of throughout the film, there's a dog

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:41.480
character — possibly a reference to the
urban legend of Sparky from the games — seen lying down.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:45.319
There's also that horrifying-looking husk
that looks suspiciously like Circus Baby that

00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:46.600
Abby is nearly put into.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:51.110
They're broken apart now, but maybe these
once housed the kids Afton took at some point.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.449
The possibility of there being more ghost
children is especially strong considering

00:05:54.449 --> 00:05:58.199
that there are a lot more characters from
the games still to make their debut.

00:05:58.199 --> 00:06:01.729
Afton's obsession with building these goofy
animatronics and putting kids in them sadly

00:06:01.729 --> 00:06:05.630
has a long history, so who knows how many
ghost kids are really out there?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.310
It's safe to say that there are more than
five.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:13.190
The ambiguity surrounding Garrett's fate makes
it very possible that he's another ghost that

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.200
Mike and Abby could meet in the near future.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.130
Although Afton admits to having taken Garrett
when Mike was a kid, he's not exactly clear

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.300
about what happened to him.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:23.610
He says that Garrett is gone, but that could
just mean that he was stuffed into one of

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:24.940
the animatronics.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:28.389
This mystery has strong potential to keep
Mike and Abby around in the franchise and

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:31.700
give them personal motivations to look for
more of Freddy's companions.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:35.440
The re-emergence of Garrett as a ghost child
also could help fill in the gaps of what happened

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:36.470
while he was with Afton.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:40.479
It could lead to more explanation of how Afton
brings these animatronics to life, as well

00:06:40.479 --> 00:06:45.479
as who he really is, especially since Afton
is largely absent throughout most of the film.

00:06:45.479 --> 00:06:49.419
Garrett could be the key to really understanding
Afton and this weird world where ghosts and

00:06:49.419 --> 00:06:52.120
machines combine to create uncanny horrors.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.540
The fates of Freddy and his pals are also
left ambiguous and could have some strong

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.010
implications for what's next in their story.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:02.319
The control that Afton has had over them is
now destroyed, so they're basically free to

00:07:02.319 --> 00:07:03.889
do whatever they want.

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:07.879
After they leave Afton to either die or become
merged with his costume, the characters could

00:07:07.879 --> 00:07:10.500
leave the place all together and find somewhere
else to call home.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.470
Maybe they go and find Abby to rekindle their
friendship.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:17.090
Or perhaps their exit from Freddy Fazbear's
Pizza could result in them visiting some of

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.960
the other locations from the games.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.680
Longtime "Five Nights at Freddy's" fans know
that as more sequels came out, the series

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:25.979
continually expanded outside of Freddy Fazbear's
Pizza.

00:07:25.979 --> 00:07:30.070
Perhaps the next film could be the right time
to bring fans to Freddy's Frights, a horror-centric

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.500
attraction that acted as the third game's
setting.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:36.180
Or, there's potential for the characters to
explore the sister location from the fifth

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:41.009
game, Circus Baby's Entertainment and Rental,
and introduce Circus Baby to the mix.

00:07:41.009 --> 00:07:44.410
The options are wide open for what Freddy
and his friends are up to, especially now

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:46.190
that they seem to be fully autonomous.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.659
"There are ghost children possessing giant
robots?

00:07:49.659 --> 00:07:52.039
Thanks for the heads up."

00:07:52.039 --> 00:07:55.979
There's currently no confirmation of a sequel
to "Five Nights at Freddy's" going into development,

00:07:55.979 --> 00:07:58.450
but the chances of it happening are very high.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:02.080
The film already made its money back before
it even hit theaters, thanks to the sale of

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.569
streaming and theatrical distribution rights.

00:08:04.569 --> 00:08:06.530
So what could happen in a potential sequel?

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:10.310
The ending of the film doesn't give many hints,
nor does the mid-credits scene, since it's

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:13.169
basically just a fun scare gag with the Balloon
Boy statue.

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:17.229
We can guess, though, that the movies will
probably continue the story of the games,

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:19.220
remixing some of the events and introductions.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:23.659
It's worth noting that the film doesn't follow
the games beat for beat, and introduces things

00:08:23.659 --> 00:08:25.970
that don't appear until later games.

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:29.760
For instance, Springtrap, who is represented
by Afton's costume choice, doesn't appear

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.039
until the third game.

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:34.539
This means that other unseen characters and
locations can appear at any point.

00:08:34.539 --> 00:08:38.500
A sequel could also weave together plot points
from the other games to create a narrative

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.620
cocktail of the franchise's best parts.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.560
So while a "Five Nights at Freddy's" sequel
is almost certainly on the horizon, it won't

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.530
exactly be predictable for fans of the games.

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:54.140
When Matthew Lillard, who plays Afton, appeared
on the WeeklyMTG podcast to talk about "Magic

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.890
the Gathering," he also revealed some interesting
information about his contract.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:09:01.550
"I just got cast in a movie called 'Five Nights
at Freddy's.'

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:05.670
It's a three-picture deal with Universal and
Blumhouse."

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:09.390
Unless Lillard is also planning to appear
in other Universal and Blumhouse projects

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:13.539
as a part of that deal, it can be assumed
that he's going to be a part of a "Five Nights" trilogy.

00:09:13.539 --> 00:09:17.149
This news lines up with director Emma Tammi's
desire to see the films be the start of a

00:09:17.149 --> 00:09:18.950
franchise she'd like to return to.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.870
Tammi told ScreenRant that there's so much
more for potential sequels to explore, saying,

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.350
"Oh, my gosh, well, the lore is massive.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:30.010
There was no way we were ever going to fit
everything into one film, nor was it the intention.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:33.880
So the answer is yes, there's so much to potentially
bring into any sequels should we be lucky

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.035
enough to make them."

00:09:35.035 --> 00:09:39.714
According to those directly involved, fans can have at least some expectation of more Five Nights At Freddy's films

00:09:39.714 --> 00:09:42.000
that delve deeper into the lore.

